  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <header>
    <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue?</h1>
    <p>天空为什么是蓝色的？</p>
  </header>

  <div class="container">

    <nav class="toggle-nav">
      <button class="toggle-btn active" onclick="showAll()">All Sections</button>
      <button class="toggle-btn" onclick="showSection(0)">🧒 Toddler</button>
      <button class="toggle-btn" onclick="showSection(1)">🎓 High School</button>
      <button class="toggle-btn" onclick="showSection(2)">🔬 PhD</button>
    </nav>

    <!-- Section 1: Toddler -->
    <div class="section" data-section="0">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>🧒 For a 3-Year-Old / 给3岁小朋友</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="columns">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-lang">English</div>
          <p>You know how when you look up during the day, the sky is blue? That's because the sun shines light down to us, and when that light hits the tiny, tiny air all around us, the blue part of the light gets splashed around everywhere — like when you splash water in a puddle! The blue splashes into your eyes from all directions, so the whole sky looks blue!</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-lang">中文</div>
          <p>宝宝你知道吗，白天我们抬头看天空，它是蓝色的！这是因为太阳把光照到我们身上，当光照到我们周围那些超级小的空气的时候，光里面蓝色的部分就被到处弹来弹去——就像你在小水坑里玩水花一样！蓝色的光从四面八方溅到你眼睛里，所以整个天空看起来就是蓝色的啦！</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 2: High School -->
    <div class="section" data-section="1">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>🎓 For a High School Teenager / 给高中生</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="columns">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-lang">English</div>
          <p>Sunlight looks white, but it's actually made up of all the colors of the rainbow (each color is a different wavelength of light). When sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it collides with gas molecules like nitrogen and oxygen.</p>
          <p>These collisions scatter the light in all directions — but not all colors equally. Shorter wavelengths (like blue and violet) scatter much more than longer wavelengths (like red and orange). This is called <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>, and the amount of scattering is proportional to 1/λ⁴ (where λ is the wavelength).</p>
          <p>So blue light gets scattered across the whole sky, and no matter where you look up, some of that scattered blue light reaches your eyes.</p>
          <p>You might wonder: "Why isn't the sky violet? Violet scatters even more!" Two reasons: the sun emits less violet light than blue, and our eyes are more sensitive to blue.</p>
          <p>At sunrise/sunset, light travels through more atmosphere, so most of the blue is scattered <em>away</em> before it reaches you — leaving the reds and oranges you see at golden hour.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-lang">中文</div>
          <p>太阳光看起来是白色的，但它其实是由彩虹的所有颜色组成的（每种颜色对应不同波长的光）。当太阳光进入地球大气层时，会与氮气、氧气等气体分子发生碰撞。</p>
          <p>这些碰撞会把光向四面八方散射——但不同颜色的散射程度不一样。波长较短的光（如蓝色和紫色）比波长较长的光（如红色和橙色）散射得多得多。这叫做<strong>瑞利散射</strong>，散射强度与 1/λ⁴ 成正比（λ 是波长）。</p>
          <p>所以蓝光被散射到整个天空中，无论你朝哪个方向抬头看，都有散射的蓝光进入你的眼睛。</p>
          <p>你可能会问："天空为什么不是紫色的？紫色散射不是更强吗？"有两个原因：太阳发出的紫光比蓝光少，而且我们的眼睛对蓝光更敏感。</p>
          <p>在日出/日落时，光线要穿过更厚的大气层，大部分蓝光在到达你眼睛之前就已经被散射<em>走了</em>——剩下的就是你在黄昏时分看到的红色和橙色。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 3: PhD -->
    <div class="section" data-section="2">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>🔬 For a Physics PhD / 给物理学博士</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="columns">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-lang">English</div>
          <p>The blue color of the sky is a consequence of <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong> of solar radiation by atmospheric molecules (primarily N₂ and O₂) whose polarizability is excited by the incident electromagnetic field.</p>
          <p>The differential scattering cross-section for a small dielectric sphere (size parameter x = 2πr/λ ≪ 1) is:</p>
          <div class="formula">dσ/dΩ = (k⁴/16π²) · [(εᵣ−1)/(εᵣ+2)]² · V² · (1 + cos²θ)</div>
          <p>where k is the wavenumber, εᵣ is the relative permittivity, V is the particle volume, and θ is the scattering angle. The total cross-section scales as λ⁻⁴, which strongly biases scattering toward the short-wavelength end of the solar spectrum.</p>
          <p>Several subtleties refine the naive picture:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Depolarization ratio</strong>: Atmospheric molecules are anisotropic scatterers, introducing a depolarization factor ρ ≈ 0.03 for N₂ that modifies the angular distribution.</li>
            <li><strong>Multiple scattering and aerosol contributions</strong>: In the real atmosphere, Mie scattering by aerosols (size parameter x ~ 1) adds an unpolarized, weakly wavelength-dependent component that desaturates the sky toward the horizon.</li>
            <li><strong>Fraunhofer absorption and ozone</strong>: The Chappuis absorption band of O₃ (centered ~600 nm) preferentially attenuates longer wavelengths in the slant path, contributing to the deep blue of the zenith at high altitudes.</li>
            <li><strong>Rayleigh optical depth</strong>: At sea level, τ_R ≈ 0.1 at 550 nm, scaling as (λ/550 nm)⁻⁴. The zenith radiance in the single-scattering approximation is L ∝ ω₀ τ_R F₀ P(Θ) / (4π).</li>
            <li><strong>Violet suppression</strong>: The solar spectral irradiance peaks near 480 nm in the visible; combined with CIE 1931 color matching functions and lens absorption, the perceived sky color lands in the cyan-blue region (~460–480 nm).</li>
          </ul>
          <p>A full treatment requires radiative transfer with multiple scattering, molecular absorption lines, and surface-boundary conditions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-lang">中文</div>
          <p>天空呈蓝色是太阳辐射被大气分子（主要是 N₂ 和 O₂）<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的结果，这些分子的极化率被入射电磁场激发。</p>
          <p>对于一个小介电球（尺寸参数 x = 2πr/λ ≪ 1），微分散射截面为：</p>
          <div class="formula">dσ/dΩ = (k⁴/16π²) · [(εᵣ−1)/(εᵣ+2)]² · V² · (1 + cos²θ)</div>
          <p>其中 k 为波数，εᵣ 为相对介电常数，V 为粒子体积，θ 为散射角。总截面按 λ⁻⁴ 标度，这强烈地将散射偏向太阳光谱的短波端。</p>
          <p>以下几个细微因素修正了这一简单图像：</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>退偏振比</strong>：大气分子是各异性散射体，引入了 N₂ 的退偏振因子 ρ ≈ 0.03，修正了角分布。</li>
            <li><strong>多重散射与气溶胶贡献</strong>：在实际大气中，气溶胶的米氏散射（尺寸参数 x ~ 1）添加了一个非偏振、弱波长依赖的分量，使天空朝地平线方向去饱和。</li>
            <li><strong>夫琅禾费吸收与臭氧</strong>：O₃ 的 Chappuis 吸收带（中心约 600 nm）在斜程路径上优先衰减较长波长，有助于高海拔地区天顶呈现深蓝色。</li>
            <li><strong>瑞利光学深度</strong>：在海平面，550 nm 处 τ_R ≈ 0.1，按 (λ/550 nm)⁻⁴ 标度。单次散射近似下天顶辐射亮度为 L ∝ ω₀ τ_R F₀ P(Θ) / (4π)。</li>
            <li><strong>紫光的抑制</strong>：大气层顶的太阳光谱辐照度在可见光区峰值位于约 480 nm；结合 CIE 1931 颜色匹配函数以及人眼晶状体对紫外/紫光的吸收，感知到的天空颜色落在青蓝色区域（主峰约 460–480 nm）。</li>
          </ul>
          <p>完整的处理需要包含多重散射的辐射传输、分子吸收线以及地表边界条件。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <script>
    function showAll() {
      document.querySelectorAll('.section').forEach(s => s.style.display = '');
      document.querySelectorAll('.toggle-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
      document.querySelectorAll('.toggle-btn')[0].classList.add('active');
    }

    function showSection(index) {
      document.querySelectorAll('.section').forEach((s, i) => {
        s.style.display = i === index ? '' : 'none';
      });
      document.querySelectorAll('.toggle-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
      document.querySelectorAll('.toggle-btn')[index + 1].classList.add('active');
    }
  </script>

</body>
</html>
"}

{"path": "earth.html", "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="ar" dir="rtl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>طبقات الأرض</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --bg1:#0b1e3a; --bg2:#061024; --ink:#f4f7fb; --muted:#a9bad4;
    --crust:#a0522d; --mantle:#c0392b; --outer:#e67e22; --inner:#f5c518;
    --accent:#5ec8ff;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
  html,body{height:100%}
  body{
    font-family:"Segoe UI","Noto Naskh Arabic","Traditional Arabic",Tahoma,system-ui,sans-serif;
    background:radial-gradient(1200px 800px at 70% -10%,#16345f 0%,var(--bg1) 45%,var(--bg2) 100%);
    color:var(--ink); overflow:hidden; line-height:1.9; -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
  }
  /* progress bar */
  .progress{position:fixed;top:0;right:0;height:4px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--accent),#8fe3ff);width:0;transition:width .4s ease;z-index:50}
  /* deck */
  .deck{position:relative;height:100vh;width:100vw}
  .slide{
    position:absolute;inset:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;
    padding:5vh 6vw;opacity:0;visibility:hidden;transform:translateY(18px) scale(.99);
    transition:opacity .5s ease,transform .5s ease,visibility .5s;
  }
  .slide.active{opacity:1;visibility:visible;transform:none}
  .kicker{color:var(--accent);letter-spacing:.15em;font-size:.85rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.4rem}
  h1{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,7vw,5rem);font-weight:800;line-height:1.2;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#fff,#bfe3ff);-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent}
  h2{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,5.5vw,3.4rem);font-weight:800;margin-bottom:.2rem}
  .sub{color:var(--muted);font-size:clamp(1rem,2.6vw,1.4rem);max-width:60ch;margin-top:.6rem}
  p.body{max-width:62ch;font-size:clamp(1rem,2.4vw,1.25rem);color:#dfe8f5}
  /* facts grid */
  .cards{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.9rem;justify-content:center;margin-top:1.4rem;max-width:900px}
  .card{background:rgba(255,255,255,.06);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);border-radius:16px;
        padding:1rem 1.2rem;min-width:150px;flex:1 1 190px;text-align:center;backdrop-filter:blur(4px)}
  .card .num{font-size:clamp(1.4rem,4vw,2.1rem);font-weight:800;color:var(--accent)}
  .card .lbl{color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;margin-top:.2rem}
  .chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;padding:.35rem .8rem;border-radius:999px;
        font-size:.9rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:1rem}
  .dot{width:.7rem;height:.7rem;border-radius:50%}
  /* diagram */
  .diagram-wrap{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:2.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1rem}
  svg.earth{width:min(64vw,340px);height:auto;filter:drop-shadow(0 18px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.5))}
  .legend{list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.7rem;text-align:right}
  .legend li{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.7rem;font-size:clamp(.95rem,2.2vw,1.15rem)}
  .legend .sw{width:1.2rem;height:1.2rem;border-radius:5px;flex:none;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px rgba(255,255,255,.15)}
  .layer{transition:opacity .4s ease,transform .4s ease;transform-origin:center}
  .dimmed{opacity:.18}
  /* table */
  table{border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:1.2rem;width:min(92vw,860px);font-size:clamp(.85rem,2vw,1.05rem)}
  th,td{padding:.7rem .6rem;text-align:center;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12)}
  thead th{color:var(--accent);font-weight:800;background:rgba(255,255,255,.05)}
  tbody tr:hover{background:rgba(255,255,255,.05)}
  td.layer-cell{font-weight:800;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;justify-content:center}
  td .sw{width:.85rem;height:.85rem;border-radius:4px}
  /* nav */
  .nav{position:fixed;bottom:1.2rem;left:0;right:0;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:1rem;z-index:50}
  .btn{cursor:pointer;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.2);background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);color:var(--ink);
       padding:.55rem 1.1rem;border-radius:999px;font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;transition:.2s;font-family:inherit}
  .btn:hover{background:rgba(255,255,255,.18);transform:translateY(-2px)}
  .btn:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:not-allowed;transform:none}
  .dots{display:flex;gap:.5rem}
  .pdot{width:.65rem;height:.65rem;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(255,255,255,.25);cursor:pointer;transition:.25s}
  .pdot.on{background:var(--accent);transform:scale(1.35)}
  .hint{position:fixed;top:.9rem;left:1rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;opacity:.7;z-index:50}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="progress" id="progress"></div>
<div class="hint">استخدم الأسهم ← → أو المسافة للتنقّل</div>

<main class="deck" id="deck">

  <!-- 1: Title -->
  <section class="slide active">
    <div class="kicker">عِلم الأحياء والكواكب</div>
    <h1>طبقات الأرض</h1>
    <p class="sub">رحلة إلى أعماق كوكبنا: من القشرة الرقيقة إلى اللبّ المعدنيّ المنصهر في المركز.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 2: Overview + diagram -->
  <section class="slide">
    <div class="kicker">نظرة عامّة</div>
    <h2>مِما تتكوّن الأرض؟</h2>
    <p class="body">تنقسم الأرض إلى أربع طبقاتٍ رئيسية تختلف في التركيب والحالة ودرجة الحرارة. نصف قطر الأرض الكامل نحو <b>6371 كم</b>.</p>
    <div class="diagram-wrap">
      <span class="earth-slot" data-hl="all"></span>
      <ul class="legend">
        <li><span class="sw" style="background:var(--crust)"></span> القشرة الأرضية</li>
        <li><span class="sw" style="background:var(--mantle)"></span> الوشاح</li>
        <li><span class="sw" style="background:var(--outer)"></span> اللبّ الخارجي</li>
        <li><span class="sw" style="background:var(--inner)"></span> اللبّ الداخلي</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3: Crust -->
  <section class="slide">
    <div class="diagram-wrap">
      <span class="earth-slot" data-hl="crust"></span>
      <div style="max-width:34ch;text-align:right">
        <div class="chip" style="background:rgba(160,82,45,.25);color:#e8c9a8"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--crust)"></span> الطبقة الخارجية</div>
        <h2>القشرة الأرضية</h2>
        <p class="body" style="text-align:right">أرقّ طبقات الأرض وأبردُها، وهي القشرة الصخرية التي نعيش عليها. تنقسم إلى <b>قارية</b> (غرانيتية) و<b>محيطية</b> (قارية) غنية بالحديد والمغنيسيوم.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cards">
